      "id": 3531195,
      "postDate": "2026-10-01T13:19:46.430Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "My first submission today failed. Kaggle showed only:  **“Notebook Threw Exception.”** \nI had no clue what went wrong or how to fix it.\nI understand why Kaggle limits logs from private test data: detailed logs could reveal information about that data. \n\nCould Kaggle first run each submission on **a small sample of public data and show the full log?**\nIf a submission fails on private data, Kaggle could still show only a general error message. This would help me tell whether the problem is in my notebook or in Kaggle’s system, while keeping the private data safe.",
      "content": "<p>My first submission today failed. Kaggle showed only:  <strong>“Notebook Threw Exception.”</strong> \nI had no clue what went wrong or how to fix it.\nI understand why Kaggle limits logs from private test data: detailed logs could reveal information about that data. </p>\n<p>Could Kaggle first run each submission on <strong>a small sample of public data and show the full log?</strong>\nIf a submission fails on private data, Kaggle could still show only a general error message. This would help me tell whether the problem is in my notebook or in Kaggle’s system, while keeping the private data safe.</p>",
